# Credentials for the backends in servers.yaml beside this file. Mode 0600; the app sets
# that on first launch and repairs it on every launch after.
#
# Grammar (see src/mcp_gateway/secrets.md -- it is small, and it will not change):
#
#   KEY=value                 raw to end of line, then stripped
#   KEY='literal'             no escapes at all
#   KEY="with\ttabs"          \n \t \r \\ \" decoded
#
#   * `#` is a legal character inside an unquoted value. There is no inline comment
#     stripping. Quote the value if you want one.
#   * A duplicate key is an ERROR naming both lines, not a silent last-wins.
#
# There is deliberately no WS_ACCESS_KEY line here. The desktop app mints its own access
# key at every launch, hands it to the gateway through the environment, and never writes it
# down -- and the environment wins over this file, so a key set here would be read, ignored,
# and quietly confusing. Nothing outside the app can reach these sockets anyway: they are
# bound to loopback on a port the app chooses at random.
#
# Referenced by servers.yaml as ${NAME}. Add what your backends need:
#
#   GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...
